---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../../utils/paths';

const pageTitle = "Native Linux & Windows Installation Guide";
const pageDesc = "Install and run AutoTelegramForward natively on Linux (Ubuntu, Debian, RHEL with systemd) and Windows using Python virtual environments.";
---

<DocsLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDesc}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Getting Started', href: url('/getting-started/') },
    { name: 'Linux & Windows', href: url('/getting-started/linux-windows/') },
  ]}
  prev={{ title: 'Docker Deployment', href: url('/getting-started/docker/') }}
  next={{ title: 'Telegram Credentials', href: url('/getting-started/telegram-bot-setup/') }}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <h2 id="linux">Linux Installation (Ubuntu / Debian / RHEL)</h2>
    <p>
      For VPS environments without Docker, AutoTelegramForward can be installed directly as a background <code>systemd</code> daemon.
    </p>

    <h3>Method A: Automated One-Line Installer</h3>
    <pre class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400"><code>curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Opselon/AutoTelegramForward/master/install.sh | bash</code></pre>

    <h3>Method B: Manual Setup</h3>
    <pre class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400"><code># 1. Install prerequisites
sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y python3 python3-venv python3-pip git

# 2. Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/Opselon/AutoTelegramForward.git
cd AutoTelegramForward

# 3. Create virtual environment
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate

# 4. Install dependencies
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 5. Populate environment variables
cp .env.example .env
nano .env

# 6. Run core
python3 -m core.main</code></pre>

    <h3>Systemd Service Configuration</h3>
    <p>
      Create <code>/etc/systemd/system/autotelegramforward.service</code>:
    </p>
    <pre class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs font-mono text-slate-300"><code>[Unit]
Description=AutoTelegramForward Engine
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=root
WorkingDirectory=/root/AutoTelegramForward
ExecStart=/root/AutoTelegramForward/.venv/bin/python3 -m core.main
Restart=always
RestartSec=5
EnvironmentFile=/root/AutoTelegramForward/.env

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target</code></pre>
    <pre class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400"><code>sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable autotelegramforward
sudo systemctl start autotelegramforward
journalctl -u autotelegramforward -f</code></pre>

    <h2 id="windows">Windows 10 / 11 / Server Installation</h2>
    <p>
      AutoTelegramForward runs smoothly on Windows using PowerShell:
    </p>

    <h3>Method A: Automated PowerShell Installer</h3>
    <pre class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400"><code>irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Opselon/AutoTelegramForward/master/install.ps1 | iex</code></pre>

    <h3>Method B: Manual PowerShell Setup</h3>
    <pre class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400"><code># 1. Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/Opselon/AutoTelegramForward.git
cd AutoTelegramForward

# 2. Create and activate venv
py -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# 3. Install requirements
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 4. Copy configuration
copy .env.example .env

# 5. Start engine
python -m core.main</code></pre>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
